<hr>
<h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Choose the correct answer from the given options.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Which of the following is the structural and functional unit of the human kidney?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Neuron</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Nephron</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Alveolus</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Malpighian tubule</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> The blood vessel that carries blood away from the glomerulus is the:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Afferent arteriole</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Renal artery</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Efferent arteriole</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Renal vein</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Which hormone acts on the collecting duct to increase water reabsorption when the body is dehydrated?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Insulin</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Antidiuretic Hormone (ADH)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Thyroxine</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Adrenaline</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> The abnormal presence of glucose in urine is known as:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Hematuria</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Glycosuria</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Uremia</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Diuresis</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Which major nitrogenous waste product is excreted in human urine?</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Uric acid</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Ammonia</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Urea</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Creatinine</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section B: Fill in the Blanks</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Fill in the blanks with appropriate terms.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> The knot of blood capillaries present inside the Bowman's capsule is called _______.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> The outer dark cortex region of the human kidney contains the _______ of nephrons.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section C: Assertion-Reason</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Select the correct option based on the Assertion and Reason provided.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Assertion (A): Ultrafiltration occurs under high hydrostatic pressure in the glomerulus.
Reason (R): The lumen of the efferent arteriole is narrower than that of the afferent arteriole.</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is not the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section D: Very Short Answer</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions briefly.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Define Osmoregulation and state its importance in the human body.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Differentiate between Glomerular Filtrate and Urine based on their chemical composition.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Name two major constituents of blood that do not pass into the Bowman's capsule during ultrafiltration. Give a reason for their absence in the filtrate.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section E: Short Answer</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions in detail.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Study the diagram of the human urinary system given below and answer the questions that follow:</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><ol style='padding-left:20px;margin-top:4px;'><li>Identify and label the parts marked as renal artery, ureter, and urinary bladder.</li><li>State the function of the ureter in the excretory process.</li><li>What is the structural difference between the male and female urethra?</li></ol><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Explain the three main physiological steps involved in urine formation: Ultrafiltration, Selective Reabsorption, and Tubular Secretion.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section F: Long Answer</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the multi-part question clearly with precise scientific explanations.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Refer to the structural diagram of a human Nephron provided below and answer the following questions:</div><div style='text-align:center;margin:8px 0;'><img src='data:image/png;base64,' style='max-width:320px;max-height:220px;' alt='Diagram'></div><ol style='padding-left:20px;margin-top:4px;'><li>Identify the parts labeled: Glomerulus, Bowman's capsule, Loop of Henle, and Collecting duct.</li><li>Describe how the structural adaptation of the capillaries in the Glomerulus enables Ultrafiltration.</li><li>Which useful substances present in the initial filtrate are selectively reabsorbed back into blood capillaries along the Proximal Convoluted Tubule (PCT)?</li><li>Define Hemodialysis and explain under what clinical condition an artificial kidney is required by a patient.</li></ol>
</body>
</html>